@startuml f6-agent-loop-fanout
title F6 — Agent loop + live event fanout (via Event Router)

|AG|
start
while (more steps?) is (yes)
  :Build prompt
   (history + tools + env);
  :POST prompt;

  |LLM|
  :Reason;
  :Return completion OR tool_use;

  |AG|
  :Receive response;

  if (Final result?) then (yes)
    :Emit final event;
    -->[handoff] "See F8 (finalize)";
    stop
  else (no, continue)
    :Execute tool (github, file, etc.);
    :Emit tool_use event
     (kind=tool_use, payload=tool, args);
  endif

  |EX|
  :Capture stdout event stream;
:REST POST /events
   to Event Router
   { task_id, kind, payload };

  |ER|
  :Persist event in ER DB;
  :Push to subscribers (GW);

  |API Gateway|
  :Proxy event frame
   to UI over WS
   (per F3 subscription);

  |Operator|
  :Receive WS push (live);
endwhile (no)

note right
  No queues. Every event from every executor
  flows through ER.
  ER pushes to GW, GW proxies to UI WS.
  Zero platform touch inside AG <-> LLM.
  GW has no logic - just proxy.
end note

stop

@enduml